  "body": "**Stacked on #1367** (branch `issue/1357-cycle-feed-spindle`). Retarget this PR to `main` before #1367 merges. Fork synced at v0.18.0; branch merged with upstream main through #1367's branch.\n\n## What changed\n- **The spindle rule in every spindle mill dialect.** #1357 gave `tormach.cps` a spindle-state rule, and the #1367 review fixed its touch-probe exemption. That rule is now ported to `fanuc`, `haas`, `sinumerik`, `mazak`, `heidenhain`, `doosan-dnm`, `grblhal`, `tinyg` and `carvera`.\n  - Each post tracks `spindleOn` from its preamble's spindle start (`S.. M3`; Mazak `MOTON S..`; Carvera `M3 S..`) to the next stop: every section end, and a touch probe's stop.\n  - A feed, arc or canned cycle with the spindle stopped is refused by name and nothing is posted for it, e.g. `feed move G1 with the spindle stopped - no spindle start (S.. M3) precedes it; state the operation's spindle speed`. One message per program.\n  - **Probe exemption:** the section must state 0 rpm **and** `PARAM ToolKind touch probe`. A cutter at 0 rpm, or a 0-rpm section that states no tool kind, is refused. The kind resets at every section end.\n  - **tinyg and carvera** write no canned cycles; their holes are plain feeds, so the feed check covers holes.\n  - **Heidenhain** checks its native cycle last, after the tapping refusals. A tap with no spindle speed keeps its own refusal (\"tapping needs a positive integral spindle speed\"). The cycle stays open, so the hole's chain is swallowed, not posted.\n- **Exempt posts:**\n  - `tormach-plasma` and `wire-iso` have no spindle.\n  - `fanuc-lathe` and `tormach-lathe` do not share the mill pattern, and they already refuse a cut with no spindle speed their own way:\n    - feed per rev (G99) needs a spindle speed;\n    - fanuc-lathe's only feed-per-minute mode (G98, C-axis live tooling) needs a live-tool speed.\n  - So no lathe post changed.\n- **Fixtures:**\n  - `conformance.rs` now posts every mill dialect's golden from `as_program` (`tests/common/legacy_program.rs`): tool change, spindle speed, setup/operation/tool comments and cycle feeds, on the same generic VMC. The pinned `.cl` files are untouched.\n  - `legacy_program::operation_for` gains a `trochoid_` arm (6 mm end mill, \"Trochoidal slot\").\n  - These hand-written streams gain a `SpindleSpeed`:\n    - post crate: `fanuc_post`, `doosan_dnm_post`, `arc_planes`, `axis_direction_cli`;\n    - app: `fourth_axis_pose`, `tinyg_post`.\n  - `heidenhain_block_form` uses `as_program`, and so does `program_units`' grbl-family test, plus the `ClearancePlane` a real stream states (both posts lift to it at a tool change).\n- **Decisions:** `docs/decisions/1359-spindle-rule-all.md`.\n\n## Goldens moved: 115 files, regenerated with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`\n**Only added lines.** Diffed with the N block numbers stripped, **0 lines were removed or changed** across all 115 files. The added lines are:\n- the setup, operation and tool comments;\n- the tool change, in each dialect's own form: `T.. M6` + `G43 H..`; Sinumerik `T.. D.. M6`; Heidenhain `T.. G17 S..`; Carvera `M6 T..`; TinyG `M5`/`M9`/lift/`T.. M6`/`M0`/frame restate;\n- the spindle start: `S.. M3`, or Mazak `MOTON S..`, Carvera `M3 S..`, Heidenhain `M3`.\n\nHeidenhain and Sinumerik renumber their N words.\n\n- **fanuc** (top level, 14): contour_disc_hole, contour_plate_with_hole, contour_tangential_lead, drill_peck, drill_plate, face_square_40x40, face_square_40x40_stepped, pocket_waterline_plate_with_island, pocket_zigzag_plate_with_island, slot_fullwidth_centerline, slot_wide_channel_rows, tap_plate, trace_plate_with_hole, trochoid_slot_small\n- **haas** (13): the 13 conformance goldens (the 13 above, without trochoid)\n- **sinumerik** (13): the same 13\n- **mazak** (13): the same 13\n- **doosan-dnm** (13): the same 13\n- **heidenhain** (12 changed + 1 new): the 12 without tap_plate changed. **`heidenhain/tap_plate.nc` is new.** That golden was a named refusal (`REFUSED`) only because the bare stream stated no spindle speed. With 500 rpm stated (the M10x1.5 tap: 750 mm/min over a 1.5 mm pitch) it posts G207, so its `REFUSED` entry is gone.\n- **grblhal** (12), **tinyg** (12), **carvera** (12): the 12 without tap_plate. tap_plate stays refused by name there: no G84, or no spindle reverse.\n- **tormach:** no golden moved.\n\n## Pins: `crates/app/tests/post_spindle_rule_all.rs`, table-driven over the 9 dialects\n- `a_feed_with_no_spindle_start_is_refused_by_name_in_every_dialect`: refused once, and the same section with a spindle speed posts clean.\n- `an_arc_with_no_spindle_start_is_refused_by_name_in_every_dialect`\n- `a_hole_with_no_spindle_start_is_refused_by_name_in_every_dialect`: a canned cycle (Heidenhain: its drilling cycle; tinyg/carvera: the plunge feed). With a spindle it posts clean.\n- `a_cutter_stating_zero_rpm_is_refused_and_a_touch_probe_is_not`: a cutter at 0 rpm and a 0-rpm section with no kind are refused; a touch probe at 0 rpm is exempt; a no-kind 0-rpm section after a probe section is refused again.\n- `a_section_after_the_stop_that_states_no_speed_is_refused`\n\n**Mutations** (the post file is edited and the pin binary re-run; every mutant is caught):\n\n| Mutant | Fails |\n|---|---|\n| Rule off (`spindleStopped` never refuses), in each of the 9 posts, one at a time | all 5 pins, each time |\n| fanuc: the cycle check dropped | the hole pin |\n| heidenhain: the cycle check dropped | the hole pin |\n| haas: the arc check dropped | the arc pin |\n| mazak: exemption on 0 rpm alone (the pre-review Tormach bug) | the 0-rpm pin |\n| grblhal: probe never exempt | the 0-rpm pin |\n| sinumerik: the tool kind not reset at section end | the 0-rpm pin (the probe-then-no-kind case) |\n| doosan-dnm: M5 not clearing `spindleOn` | the section-after-stop pin |\n| tinyg: M3 not setting `spindleOn` | 3 pins |\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` at b0d50c6f is green: post suites ok, app suites ok (548 s).\n- camcraft-post: all suites pass.\n- App: `conformance`, `post_spindle_rule_all`, `post_cycle_feed_spindle`, `tinyg_post`, `fourth_axis_pose` and `golden_cl` pass. Before the merge of main, the whole camcraft-app test set (every binary) ran green after the two fixture fixes.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The `--ignored` heavy lanes and the release-tier UI snapshot lane.\n- **No controller run.** The changed goldens are for the generic VMC dialects, not the 770MX, so no Hub run applies.\n- A mid-section `SpindleSpeed` change still takes effect only at the next preamble. This was pre-existing and is unchanged here.\n\nChangelog: Every spindle mill post (Fanuc, Haas, Siemens 840D, Mazak, Heidenhain, Doosan DNM, grblHAL, TinyG, Carvera) refuses a feed, arc or canned cycle with the spindle stopped by name; a touch-probe section is exempt only on a touch-probe tool.\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1359\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
